Z||000000||JohnF||10-21-2001||08:29 PM||||I will soon replace the "headrest" speaker seats with non-speaker seats in my '85.  Any problems with door or aft column cover speakers (as in '88) for the "rear" sound?  Recommendations for speakers?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jncomutt||10-21-2001||08:36 PM||||I replaced my headrest speaker with 3.5" Boston Acoustics.  I don't recall the exact model #, I think CX3 or CX4, something like that.  They're not competion quality but my factory ones sounded like shredded tracing paper.  They don't have quite the mid-low that the factory ones had new,(due to bass-blockers for safe keeping) but as far as the mid-high, they're great and crystal clear!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pheagey||10-21-2001||08:43 PM||||Hey there, someelse settin' up a system in there Fiero hua?<BR>   I'd recomment Boss/Pioneer speaker any day of the week. check out Pioneers site @ <A HREF="http://www.pioneerelectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pioneerelectronics.com</A>  I've never had any complaints about Pioneer stuff..<BR>(Home system:<BR>Receiver: SA-6500 II,<BR>Amp: TX-6500 II,<BR>Speaker: CS-K531.<BR>Car system:<BR>Head Unit: DEH-75PDH.)<P>------------------<BR>Pheagey Grean<BR>"The time to talk is over. The time for diplomacy is over, the time for bluffing is over. The time to kick some f!@king as$ is now."<P>'88 coupe 'Hotwheels'<P>Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html<P>Kills: '97 Civic Auto,<BR>Killed by: -||||reg||12
Z||000003||Oreif||10-21-2001||08:47 PM||||To mount speakers in the sail panels on 84 or 85 cars, You need to cut the metal. A decent 4" speaker will fit. If you want to make a plate you can fit a 5 1/4" up there too. The reason you need to make a mounting plate is the depth of some 5 1/4" speakers is huge. Just cut out the size you need and set them in. It is difficult to cut with a saw. You might try a Roto-Zip. The problem is depth. Most saws will bottom out when cutting.  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
